<!--
  Playground snippets are compiled against the metadata of the trimmed framework that ships with the app, so a
  member the gallery never calls would otherwise be missing at compile time (for example the
  DefaultInterpolatedStringHandler.AppendFormatted(value, format) overload behind every $"{x:F2}").
  These are the System.Private.CoreLib types a snippet commonly touches; they are kept whole.
  (System.Runtime, System.Console, System.Linq and System.Collections are rooted whole in the .csproj.)
-->
